<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Devlet I Giray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1512–1577</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Devlet I Giray was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> from 1551 to 1577. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, he waged war on Muscovy, and in 1571 his army reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and burned much of the city. His attempt to repeat the invasion in 1572 ended in heavy defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-molodi">Battle of Molodi</a> south of Moscow.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/devlet-i-giray.jpg" alt="Devlet I Giray" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matrakçı Nasuh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devlet_I_Giray.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
